# Vehicle/CAN scan reports and getter dumps — device fingerprints, keep them local
dwm-vehicle-scan*.txt
DWM vehicle scan*.txt
DWM CAN getters*.txt

# Photos of the deck dropped in for debugging — they show the car interior and
# are not project files. Screenshots of those photos count: the one that prompted
# v0.44.0 has a live map with the owner's position on it and a reflection of the
# owner in the glass.
IMG_*.jpg
IMG_*.jpeg
IMG_*.png
Screenshot *.png

# Reference frames of the stock launcher hosting a live app (the com.dofun.variety
# lead in CLAUDE.md). Kept locally, never published: they are frames from someone
# else's demo video, and "ex 1.png" has a saved home address on the Waze panel.
# Same call as the declined Sketchfab model — unverifiable licence in a public repo.
ex *.png

# The stock launcher hosting live CarPlay, which is what proved the freeform route in
# v0.35.0. Same call again: it is a watermarked product photo from a reseller's listing,
# so it is evidence to work from and not ours to republish.
Picsart-*.webp

# A whole second copy of this project, extracted from "DWM context.zip" during the
# 2026-08-08 machine move. Its one unique file, "context DWM.md", is merged into
# CLAUDE.md. Never track it: it carries a duplicate release keystore, and the nested
# local.properties would slip past the root-anchored /local.properties rule above.
/DWM context/

# Vendor APKs pulled off the deck for decompiling. *.apk already covers them;
# named explicitly so nothing else in here (dumps, notes) gets published either.
# The vendor's .aidl files ARE committed, under app/src/main/aidl — those are the
# interface definition we build against, not redistributed binaries.
extracted apps/
